 #:seon.task{:name "arity-caches-copy-the-indexes"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.db/arity-commit-cache holds 92.6 MB at idle: two bases of 54 and 38 MB (one with 99,659 edges, 7,518 callers, 4,927 callees), whose edge-set, by-caller and by-callee copy what the EAVT index and the :seon.fn/calls AVET index already hold; bases evicted from arity-base-cache (LRU 4) stay alive in the commit cache (LRU 16); the content key holds 78k-datom vectors that keep loose datoms alive (1.48 M loose datoms, 160 MB heap-wide). Keep only candidates, checked, edges and bounds per value and read callers and callees from the indexes. Measured again 2026-09-28 (default, seon.cache/status): the three arity kinds hold 458 of the cache's 503 MB weighted bytes (arity-base 283 MB, 39 hits / 131 misses; arity-revision 175 MB, 14 hits / 211 misses; the same base objects are weighed once per kind that holds them), evicting everything else (decoded-edn 22,054 evictions); arity-base rebuilds from the whole program per write revision (116 calls, 142 ms mean, 1.3 s max). The gate is whole-program work per change: check only the edges a write touches (callers among the written definitions, and callers of written callees via the :seon.fn/calls AVET index), keep no whole-program base, and delete the three kinds."
             :must-read #{seon.db/arity-mismatches}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/mem-idle-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "custody-scopes-widen"
