 #:seon.task{:name "a-report-db-before-names-a-stale-commit"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A transaction report's :db-before is the writer's uncommitted previous value, whose commit id is the branch point (three writes on one branch: every :db-before named the same commit, E2; writer.cljc:210). accept-merge! records (db/commit-id (:db-before report)) as :seon.source/base-commit-id, so the accepted value names a stale base (merge-test). Derive the base from the committed :db-after's parents minus the merged parents, and make commit-id refuse or name an uncommitted value instead of answering a stale id."
             :must-read #{seon.db/commit-id seon.cluster.source/accept-merge!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/red-triage-r6-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "q-lets-a-dependency-throw-escape"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.db/q threw a raw NullPointerException from Datahike's post-filter-not-joins instead of answering an error value (lowering fixed in f7a664c2f, E3). Catch the dependency's throw at the owner and answer the declared read refusal carrying the whole cause chain."
